# Cutting plane x+y+z = 0.999, passing 0.001 units from three vertices of clay_unit_cube.
#
# Tests the numerical boundary around "is this intersection point an existing vertex?"
# in convertIntersectionToIpoints.  The plane x+y+z=1 would pass exactly through
# three cube vertices (1,1,-1), (1,-1,1), (-1,1,1) — see knife_through_3verts.obj.
# This plane is 0.001 units away, so those near-vertex intersections should NOT
# be classified as clay vertices (they fall outside the POINT_ULP tolerance).
#
# Useful for checking that the ULP threshold doesn't over-eagerly snap nearby
# new points onto existing mesh vertices, which would produce wrong geometry.

v  3 -1 -1.001
v -1  3 -1.001
v -1 -1  2.999

f 1 2 3
